        "transcriptHtml": "<p class=\"transcript-note\">Automatic transcript. It may contain small recognition errors; the answer key is authoritative.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[00:00]</span> Test one. Section one. You will hear a woman being interviewed by a market researcher in a health club about her membership of the club. First, you have some time to look at questions one to five. Now we shall begin. You should answer the questions as you listen, because you will not hear the recording a second time.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[00:46]</span> Listen carefully and answer questions one to five. Excuse me. I wonder if you&#x27;d have the time to take part in some market research. Um, what&#x27;s it about? About this club and your experiences and opinions about being a member. It&#x27;ll take less than five minutes.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[01:08]</span> Oh, okay then. As long as it&#x27;s quick. Can I start by taking your name? It&#x27;s Selena Thompson. Is that T-H-O-M-P-S-O-N?</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[01:22]</span> Yes. Okay. Great. Thanks.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[01:26]</span> And what do you do for a living? Well, I&#x27;m an accountant, but I&#x27;m between jobs at the moment. I understand. But that&#x27;s the job I&#x27;ll put down on the form. And would you mind my asking which age group you fall into?</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[01:43]</span> Below 30, 31 to 50, and above. Over 50. I think we can safely say. Great. Thanks.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[01:54]</span> And which type of membership do you have? Sorry. I&#x27;m not sure what you mean. Do you mean how long of no? Is it a single person membership? Oh, right. No, it&#x27;s a family membership.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[02:06]</span> Thanks. And how long have you been a member? Oh, let me see. I was certainly here five years ago, and it was probably two to three years more than that.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[02:20]</span> Mm-hmm. Shall I put down eight? Oh, I remember now. It&#x27;s nine, definitely. Sorry. No problem. I&#x27;ve got that.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[02:29]</span> And the last question in this first part is what brought you to the club? Sorry. How did you find out about the club? Did you see any ads? Well, I did, actually. But I have to say, I wasn&#x27;t really attracted to the club because of that.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[02:45]</span> It was through word of mouth. So you were recommended by a friend? Actually, my doctor. I&#x27;d been suffering from high blood pressure. And he said the club was very supportive of people with that condition.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[02:58]</span> So I signed up. Mm-hmm. Great. Thanks. Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions six to ten. Now listen and answer questions six to ten.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[03:33]</span> Now, for the second part of the form, I want to ask a bit more about your experience of the club. Sure. How often would you say you use the club? Oh, it varies enormously, depending on how busy I am.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[03:47]</span> Of course. But on average per month? I&#x27;d say it averages out at twice a week. Okay. So eight on average? Yeah. And four of those are aqua aerobics classes.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[04:01]</span> That leads me to the next question. Would you say the swimming pool is the facility you make most use of? Mm-hmm. Fair to say that. Yep. Right. Thanks.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[04:12]</span> And are there any facilities you don&#x27;t use? Mm-hmm. One area I realize I&#x27;ve never used is the tennis courts. Mm-hmm.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[04:23]</span> And there&#x27;s one simple reason for that. You don&#x27;t play tennis? Actually, I&#x27;m not bad at it. Oh.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[04:29]</span> It&#x27;s that I&#x27;m not happy having to pay extra for that privilege. Oh, right. I&#x27;ve made a note of that. Thanks. Mm-hmm.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[04:38]</span> Now, in the last section, are there any suggestions or recommendations you have for improvements to the club? Only about health and fitness. Mm-hmm. Anything at all? Well, I&#x27;d like to see more social events.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[04:53]</span> Oh. It isn&#x27;t just a question of getting together for games or classes, but other things, you know? Yes, sure. And another thing that I was thinking when I had my yoga class in the gym last night, we were all sweltering in the heat.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[05:08]</span> Uh, was that I think they should put in, well, you know... Air conditioning. That&#x27;s exactly what I mean. The rooms are really light and well-designed, but they do need proper installations.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[05:21]</span> Sure. Well, I&#x27;ve made a note of that. Good. So, is there anything else you&#x27;d like to suggest about quality of service, for example? Oh, everyone&#x27;s very nice here.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[05:34]</span> They couldn&#x27;t be more friendly and helpful. Oh, but I tell you what, it&#x27;s a shame the restaurant isn&#x27;t open in the evening on Saturday. And Sunday is well for that matter. Oh.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[05:46]</span> So, the club should... Open it later on those days. Okay. Well, thank you very much. That&#x27;s all the questions I have.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[05:55]</span> That is the end of section one. You now have half a minute to check your answers. Now turn to section two. Test one.</p>"
